# connerlabPKI Root CA: the root of the lab's own certificate authority. The
# Forgejo's certificate chains to it. It is a public certificate, not a
# secret. flake.nix adds it to the CA bundle of the one derivation that
# downloads Go modules, so that go and git can fetch
# forgejo.kube.internal.conn3r.xyz/connerlab/termsafe; nothing else trusts it
# through this file.
#
#   subject      O=connerlabPKI, CN=connerlabPKI Root CA
#   valid        2025-09-24 to 2035-09-22
#   sha256       D8:0B:66:B2:9A:B6:DD:76:0E:86:34:76:09:99:30:1A:55:79:FE:0F:33:71:37:70:D6:59:71:7F:F4:E7:29:5A
#   copied from  nixos-config, certs/root_ca.crt, which is the copy the hosts trust
#
# When the root is replaced, replace this file in every repository that
# fetches from the Forgejo inside a Nix build. Check a new copy with
#   openssl x509 -in nix/connerlab-root-ca.crt -noout -subject -dates -fingerprint -sha256
